Certainly! Here's a LabVIEW program that simulates the effects of a stun gun shock:

```labview
// Input: Voltage of the stun gun (in volts)
// Output: Time-varying voltage representing the electrical stimulation

// Create a new waveform generator with a sampling rate of 10 MHz and a duration of 10 milliseconds
WaveformGen, Create, SampleRate 10e6, Duration 10e-3

// Set the waveform to a square wave with the input voltage and a rise time of 1 microsecond
WaveformGen.Waveform = SquareWave, Voltage 0, Amplitude InputVoltage, RiseTime 1e-6

// Output the waveform to a virtual instrument representing the electrical stimulation
VIWrite, "StimulationOutput", WaveformGen.Output

// Wait for the simulation to finish
Wait, 10e-3

// Stop the waveform generator
WaveformGen.Stop

// Release the waveform generator
Delete, WaveformGen
```

**Note:** This is just a simulation and does not represent the actual effects of a real stun gun.
